# ==============================================================================
# Line-ending policy. This file is not boilerplate — it is load-bearing.
#
# Git on Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF in
# the working copy on checkout. This project has already been bitten by that
# once: a JavaScript file with mixed line endings fails to parse in the browser
# with no console error at all, and the entire script block silently does
# nothing. Because deploys go up by FTP rather than by git pull, a normalized
# CRLF working copy would be uploaded verbatim to the server and reintroduce
# exactly that failure.
#
# Forcing eol=lf means every checkout on every platform matches what the server
# expects, regardless of the developer's local git settings.
# ==============================================================================

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries git must never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gpx binary
*.db  binary
